## Commits
### 87c8823
perf(state): add array fill benchmark case for the baseline

The wrap-fill-and-copywithin change alters how many wakes one fill call
causes. This case subscribes one effect that reads every index of a
hookless array and times fill calls that change every element, so the
unchanged library records the baseline. Typed perf because it measures
performance; no library behaviour changes.


